    text: "Accessories and jewellery are the finishing touches that complete an outfit and express personal style. Jewellery includes rings, necklaces, bracelets, and earrings — items worn for adornment, often made from precious metals like gold and silver, and set with gemstones such as diamonds, rubies, and emeralds. A wedding ring symbolizes marriage, while an engagement ring marks a proposal. Watches serve both function and fashion — from a simple digital watch to a luxury timepiece. Brooches and pins add elegance to jackets and scarves. Beyond jewellery, everyday accessories include belts, bags, wallets, and sunglasses. A handbag or shoulder bag carries daily essentials, while a briefcase signals professionalism. Hats, caps, and headbands offer both style and protection. Hair accessories like clips, pins, and scrunchies keep hair neat. Scarves and shawls can be both fashionable and functional. In colder months, gloves, mittens, and earmuffs keep extremities warm. The vocabulary of accessories extends to materials — leather, silk, velvet, suede — and to fasteners: clasps, buckles, zippers, and buttons. Understanding these terms helps when shopping, describing outfits, and appreciating the craftsmanship behind beautiful accessories.",
